ast Germans head on, and was only 16th in the world in 1987. In the prelims Hörner confirmed her fitness, leading in 2:27.63, within ½-second of Higson’s world mark, while Higson qualified fourth."] "\n\n" [:p {} "In the final, the pace through 100 metres was set by Bulgarian " [:a {:href "/athletes/45698"} "Tanya Dangalakova"] ", who was recovering from having a baby in June 1987, and having surgery related to it in October 1987. But then Hörner took over, winning in a world record 2:26.71, well ahead of China’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/46080"} "Huang Xiaomin"] ". Dangalakova could not hang on, placing fourth, also behind her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/45702"} "Antoaneta Frenkeva"] ", but she would recover and win the 100 breast in a few days, upsetting Hörner. Higson was never a factor in this race, placing seventh."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "B Final"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "172"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/47482"} "Silke Hörner"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "2:27.63 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:26.71 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "73"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/46080"} "Huang Xiaomin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CHN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CHN.png"}] "CHN"]] [:td {} "2:30.03 (3 h5)"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "2:27.49 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "46"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athlete